WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.240
Now it is time for everyone to get hands-on and start building that muscle

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:10.040
memory. Please head over to your mannequins in your small groups. For this

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:14.520
exercise, we want no more than three students per mannequin to make sure

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:19.799
everyone gets plenty of time to practice. Our goal for this session is simple but

00:00:19.799 --> 00:00:25.719
vital. Focus on consistency and rhythm. Remember, chest compressions are the most

00:00:25.719 --> 00:00:30.280
important action you can take for someone in cardiac arrest. We are looking

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:34.240
for four key things. Correct hand placement centered on the sternum,

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:40.000
pushing to a depth of at least two inches, maintaining a rate of 100 to 120

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:45.320
beats per minute, and allowing that chest to fully recoil every single time. While

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:48.959
you work, your instructor will play a steady beat to help you keep the right

00:00:48.959 --> 00:00:53.360
pace and give each of you enough time to perform three full sets of 30

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:58.919
compressions. As you do your compressions, please count out loud. It really helps

00:00:58.919 --> 00:01:02.959
you stay focused and prevents you from losing track in the heat of the moment.

00:01:02.959 --> 00:01:07.879
Your instructor will be moving around the room to offer feedback. Go ahead and

00:01:07.879 --> 00:01:12.519
start your sets now. Push to the beat, use your shoulders, and let that chest

00:01:12.519 --> 00:01:16.680
expand fully between every push.

